# AGENTS.md — {{PROJECT}} (ProductVideos)

Always-on guidance for AI coding agents (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex) working in this repository. Generated by `platform-product-video-harness` `/init-workspace`; edit the harness templates, not this file directly (re-running `/init-workspace --scaffold-tools` will offer to refresh it).

## Repo purpose

This is the **{{PROJECT}} ProductVideos** workspace — a Remotion project + brand kit + per-video project folders. The `platform-product-video-harness` plugin (in the `harness-platform` marketplace on GitHub: `ameenaliu/harness-platform`) reads + writes here to produce product videos for social media.

- **Workspace**: local folder, optionally backed by a GitHub repo: `{{REPO_URL}}` (leave blank for a purely local workspace)
- **Default branch**: `main`
- **Default voice ID**: `{{VOICE_ID}}` ({{VOICE_TONE}})
- **Default target duration**: {{TARGET_DURATION_SECONDS}}s

## Credentials — `.env` (never committed, never auto-written)

The ElevenLabs API key lives in `<repo-root>/.env` as `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...`. Hard rules:

- **NEVER edit `.env` programmatically.** The `secrets-guard.sh` hook blocks it. The user maintains `.env` in their text editor.
- **NEVER paste an API key into source code.** The `secrets-guard.sh` hook catches `sk_…40+hex` patterns at Write/Edit time.
- **NEVER commit `.env`.** `.gitignore` excludes it; the hook also rejects `git add .env*` / `git commit*` with `.env*` staged.
- **Rotate immediately** if a key ever leaks: revoke at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys, generate a new one, scrub from git history.

If a workflow needs the key and it's missing, halt with the standardised remediation block (see `.agents/skills/env-credential-recipes/SKILL.md` for the canonical text).

## Branding — `brand/brand.json` is single source of truth

All colors, fonts, logo placement come from `brand/brand.json`. NEVER hardcode hex / font names in `compositions/`. The `reviewer` agent rejects compositions with hardcoded brand tokens as `[V5-CRITICAL]`.

## Brand voice (in script copy)

- Use the brand's personas from `brand.json` (`brand.personas[].key`) — never a generic "user" unless that's literally the persona label. (The neutral starter set is `end_user`, `prospect`, `partner`.)
- Banned words / phrases come from `brand.tone.banned_*` (starter set: `revolutionary`, `game-changing`, `disrupt`, `synergy`, `leverage`, `10x`, `AI-powered`, `next-generation`, `world-class`).
- Preferred CTA verbs come from `brand.tone.preferred_verbs` (plus the usual `download`, `try`, `get`, `visit`, `learn`, `sign up`, `start`).

## Workflow — single command, 5 phases, 3 gates

```
/platform-product-video-harness:generate projects/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<slug>
```

| Phase | Job | Gate |
|---|---|---|
| 1 Analyze | ffmpeg + Claude vision read sample.mp4 → analysis.json | — |
| 2 Script | scriptwriter picks template, drafts script.md | GATE #1 |
| 3 Build | compositor writes .tsx, renders 3 silent previews | GATE #2 |
| 4 Narrate | ElevenLabs TTS + SFX BGM + ffmpeg mux → 3 final MP4s | — |
| 5 Review | reviewer ffprobes each output | GATE #3 |

Output: `projects/<slug>/out/{9-16,1-1,16-9}.mp4` — manual posting to social media.

## Production principles (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

These rules are encoded in the harness plugin at `agents/shared/video-production-principles.md` (Claude Code loads it directly; for Codex they're inlined into each subagent's `developer_instructions` via the compositor/reviewer role bodies). Key rules the reviewer enforces:

- Brand tokens always (no hardcoded hex / fonts)
- Captions burned in for every voiceover line
- Audio: -16 LUFS voiceover, -28 LUFS BGM bed
- Hook in first 3 seconds (Scene 1)
- CTA verb in final scene
- Compositions ≤ 150 lines (extract reusable to `compositions/_components/`)
- Duration within ±2s of script target
- No raw `<div>` / `<img>` (use Remotion primitives + `_components/`)
- Aspect-ratio safe zones (`<SafeArea>` handles this)

